   input:'Accessible straight-edged triangles and rectangles have complete supplied side/vertex/right-angle property descriptions. The instructor teaches closed boundary, sides and vertices, and identifies a rectangle from four sides and four right angles, including a rotated example. Right-angle templates are supplied; no unaided angle reading or trigonometry is inferred.',
   task:'Inspect/direct the supplied property checks, explain why rotation or colour does not change the defined shape and distinguish a similar-looking open boundary or non-right-angle quadrilateral. Preserve unknown properties rather than name a shape from appearance alone.',
